    {
      "content": "1. The number of dishes each student makes does not affect the amount of clay needed for **one dish**.\n2. Each clay dish requires **2 cups of clay**.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\text{ cups}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: Kora makes 20 clay dishes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. Kora makes 20 dishes, and Rory makes 20 more, so Rory makes 40 dishes.\n2. However, the problem states that **each dish requires 2 cups of clay**.\n3. Thus, for one dish, each student needs:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\text{ cups}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many total clay dishes do Jada and Rory make together?",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. Kora makes 20 dishes.\n2. Rory makes 20 more than Kora:\n\n\\[\n20+20=40\n\\]\n\n3. Jada makes twice as many as Rory:\n\n\\[\n2\\times 40=80\n\\]\n\n4. Together, Jada and Rory make:\n\n\\[\n80+40=\\boxed{120\\text{ clay dishes}}\n\\]",
